---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Scene from '../components/Scene.astro';
import { buy } from '../config';
---

<Base title="Our family" description="Diapontia comes from one family olive grove on the north-west coast of Corfu, facing the Diapontian islands.">
  <article class="page">
    <div class="page-scene"><Scene uid="story" /></div>
    <h1>Our family’s grove</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Our olive trees have been in the family for hundreds of years. They grow on the north-west coast of Corfu,
      where the land meets the Ionian Sea and the Diapontian islands sit on the horizon.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each generation has cared for the same groves and passed them on to the next. This bottle holds their oil,
      harvested and pressed on the island, and shared with you as it has always been shared at our table.
    </p>
    <!-- TODO: Yiannis, add one or two true family details here: who planted or tended the trees, harvest memories. -->

    <h2>The name</h2>
    <p>
      Othonoi, Ereikoussa and Mathraki are the Diapontian islands, off the north-west tip of Corfu. From the grove you
      see them on the horizon. The label shows that view: one old tree, the sea, and Othonoi and Diaplo in the distance.
    </p>

    <h2>How we make sure it is extra virgin</h2>
    <p>
      “Extra virgin” is a legal grade, not a description. An independent laboratory tests every batch before it is
      bottled. Only oil that meets the extra virgin standard carries the Diapontia name.
    </p>

    <h2>Bottled in Greece, packed in the UK</h2>
    <p>
      A bottler in Greece fills and labels each 750 ml bottle. The bottles travel to the UK, where we keep them somewhere
      cool and dark and pack every order by hand.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:2.5rem"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={buy.one.url}>Order a bottle<span class="price-tag">£{buy.one.price}</span></a></p>
  </article>
</Base>
